\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. We give Thee but Thine own,
\par Whate'er the gift may be;
\par All that we have is Thine alone;
\par A trust, O Lord, from Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. May we Thy bountless thus
\par As stewards true receive,
\par And gladly, as Thoun blessest us,
\par To Thee our first- fruits give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O hearts are bruised and dead,
\par And homes are bare and cold;
\par And lambs, for whom the Shepherd bled,
\par Are straying from the fold..
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To comfort and to bless,
\par To find a balm for woe,
\par To tend the lone and fatherless
\par Is angel's work below.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The captive to release,
\par To God the lost to bring,
\par To teach the way of life and peace,
\par It is a Christ- like thing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And we believe Thy word,
\par Though dim our faith may be;
\par Whate'er for Thine we do, O Lord,
\par We do it unto Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

